      "file_path": "tools/thumbs.py",
      "line_number": 8,
      "line_end": 9,
      "title": "Shell command built from the uploaded file name",
      "description": "make_thumbnail interpolates upload_name into a shell string and runs it with shell=True. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form, so the user controls it. An uploader can name a file with a semicolon or backticks and run any command on the server. A name with ../ also writes outside the thumbs directory. Validate upload_name as a bare file name, then call subprocess.run with an argument list and no shell.",
      "suggested_change": "subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "make_thumbnail interpolates upload_name into a shell string and runs it with shell=True. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form, so the user controls it.",
      "consequence": "An uploader can name a file with a semicolon or backticks and run any command on the server. A name with ../ also writes outside the thumbs directory.",
      "fix": "Validate upload_name as a bare file name, then call subprocess.run with an argument list and no shell."
    },
